Because the effect depends on an object literal that is re-created every render.

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  load(options);
}, [options]);
```

messages.text:
Because the effect depends on an object literal that is re-created every render.
useEffect(() => {
load(options);
}, [options]);

messages.markdown:
Memoise the object or depend on its primitive fields:

```jsx
const stable = useMemo(() => ({ id }), [id]);
useEffect(() => { load(stable); }, [stable]);
```

